            <div xml:id="d496">

                <pb facs="0498" n="489" sameAs="frus:frus1938v05/pg489"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">837.51 Public Works Debt/151: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Cuba</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Wright</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Habana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-11-02T14:00:00-05:00">November 2, 1938—2
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received November 2—1:35 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>132. Montoulieu yesterday confirmed in writing to Mr. Crafts the general
                    agreement outlined in the Embassy’s telegram No. 130, November 1, 1 p.m. Mr.
                    Crafts in a letter to the Cuban Ambassador yesterday likewise confirmed general
                    agreement subject to working out of details. Cuban Ambassador told Mr. Crafts
                    last night the President had approved agreement. Montoulieu and Gorrin<anchor
                        n="37" xml:id="d496-f1"/> are working out details of new taxes.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wright</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d496-f1" n="37" xml:id="d496-f1-content">
                <p>Attorney for the Chase National Bank.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
